# ─── Frontend → gateway wiring: committed defaults ────────────────────────────
# Personal overrides belong in .env.local (gitignored by the *.local rule).
# Never put a secret in any of these files: anything named VITE_* is inlined
# into the public browser bundle at build time.

# Where the Python gateway listens. Read ONLY by vite.config.ts to aim the dev
# proxy — it has no VITE_ prefix, so it never reaches the browser bundle.
# Keep in sync with GATEWAY_PORT in gateway/.env.local (default 8020).
GATEWAY_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8020

# Dev server port for this app.
FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# Prefix the browser puts in front of every gateway path. `/backend` is where the
# gateway registers its JSON API (see API_PREFIX in gateway/app.py); a call site
# writes api.get('/dashboard/me') and it goes to /backend/dashboard/me.
#
# A path (not an origin) keeps every request same-origin, which is a requirement
# here rather than a convenience: the gov_session cookie is HttpOnly and
# SameSite=Strict (gateway/app.py:910), so no JS can attach it by hand and a
# genuinely cross-site request would not send it at all. Correct in both modes —
# dev via server.proxy, prod because the gateway serves this bundle itself.
#
# To point at a gateway on another host later, make this absolute and keep the
# suffix: https://gateway.example.com/backend (also needs CORS + SameSite=None).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/backend
